# Example Mapping

Behavioral source of truth: [`docs/examples/README.md`](../../docs/examples/README.md) and maps under `docs/examples/ui/` / `docs/examples/runtime/`.

## Before coding (UI / feature work)

1. Open or create the relevant map (story / rules / examples / questions / out of scope).
2. Unresolved **Questions** are red cards — batch-ask (`ask-on-ambiguity`); do not silently invent consequential behavior.
3. Every new or changed **Example** cites a real `Test: path::fn` and that test is added or updated in the same change.
4. Prefer widget-local `#[cfg(test)]`; full-app harness only when shell wiring is required (`egui-interaction-testing` skill).

## Do not

- Duplicate scenario prose into `.mdc` rules or skills — keep thin pointers to maps
- Ship greens without tests
- Grow hub types to “make the map easier” when a narrower module works (`crate-boundaries`)
